  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{2}{12}$ on the left and $\\frac{8}{12}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129810/assets/1ff8622e7061b4bf8231b3d6dbe7eaab2199b00cc96530b7b3a2d63a1b31b169.png)\n\nThe shape on the left has $2$ shaded pieces, and the shape on the right has $8$ shaded pieces. So the number of shaded pieces has increased by a factor of $4.$\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{12}\\times 4=\\frac{8}{12}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $4.$",
